# scripts/guardian-prompt-lock.mjs hashes the raw bytes of JUDGE_A_SYSTEM/
# JUDGE_B_SYSTEM read straight off disk. core.autocrlf=true (the common
# Windows default) checks these files out with CRLF locally while the
# committed blob (and every Linux CI runner) is LF -- same logical content,
# different hash, so a Windows contributor running `lock:guardian:up` can
# silently lock against the wrong bytes and pass locally while failing
# gk-007-static on push. Forcing LF for exactly the lock-sensitive files
# closes that gap without touching line-ending behavior anywhere else in
# the repo.
lib/dualGuardian.ts text eol=lf
scripts/adversarial-probe.mjs text eol=lf
scripts/.guardian-prompts.lock text eol=lf
scripts/guardian-prompt-lock.mjs text eol=lf
